---
if (__CI_ENV__ === "live") return new Response(null, { status: 404 });

import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Select";
---

<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <div class="docs-page">
    <nav><a href="/dd_e2e/">&larr; Test Pages</a></nav>
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Select</h1>

      <p>
        A dropdown that opens a styled menu below its button, matching the Hugo
        Bootstrap dropdown used for the Language and Datadog site selectors. It
        replaces the native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>, whose popup is drawn by
        the operating system: on macOS it opens over the current value and
        ignores CSS.
      </p>

      <p>
        It follows the WAI-ARIA listbox button pattern. The button opens the
        menu on click, <kbd>Enter</kbd>, <kbd>Space</kbd>, or <kbd>&darr;</kbd>.
        In the menu, <kbd>&uarr;</kbd>/<kbd>&darr;</kbd>, <kbd>Home</kbd>, and
        <kbd>End</kbd> move the highlight, <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd>
        chooses, and <kbd>Escape</kbd>, <kbd>Tab</kbd>, or a click outside
        closes it.
      </p>

      <p>
        State and persistence live in the consuming component (for example,
        <code>RegionSelector</code> keeps the region in a cookie);
        <code>Select</code> only renders the control and reports the chosen value.
      </p>

      <h2>Properties</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr
            ><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th
            ></tr
          >
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            ><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>&mdash;</td
            ><td
              >Applied to the button. Also prefixes the listbox and option IDs.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>labelledBy</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td
              >&mdash;</td
            ><td
              >ID of the visible label element. Screen readers announce the
              label, then the current value.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>options</code></td><td
              ><code>{"{ value: string; label: string }[]"}</code></td
            ><td>&mdash;</td><td>The choices, in display order.</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td
              >&mdash;</td
            ><td>The current value.</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>onChange</code></td><td
              ><code>(value: string) =&gt; void</code></td
            ><td>&mdash;</td><td
              >Called with the chosen value, only when it differs from <code
                >value</code
              >.</td
            ></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>BEM classes</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Class</th><th>Element</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            ><td><code>select</code></td><td
              >Outer wrapper. Its <code>data-value</code> holds the current value;
              tests should read state here.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>select--open</code></td><td
              >Modifier on the wrapper while the menu is open. Flips the
              chevron.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>select__button</code></td><td
              >The button that shows the current value.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>select__menu</code></td><td
              >The listbox. Has the <code>hidden</code> attribute while closed.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>select__option</code></td><td
              >One choice. Its <code>data-value</code> holds the option value.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>select__option--selected</code></td><td
              >The option that matches the current value.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td><code>select__option--active</code></td><td
              >The highlighted option, from pointer hover or arrow keys.</td
            ></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Live examples</h2>

      <p>Two consumers render the component:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>LanguageSelector</code> — in the API toolbar.</li>
        <li>
          <code>RegionSelector</code> — see the <a
            href="/dd_e2e/components/region-selector/">Region Selector</a
          > test page.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .docs-page {
    max-width: 960px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
  }

  h1 {
    border-bottom: var(--border-width-thick) solid var(--color-border-strong);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
